er. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_end The second endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. integer, intent(in) :: n The number of dependent variables represented by the interpolant. procedure, public :: set_dense_output_enabled => oi_set_dense_enabled Enables dense output on every accepted step (default: false). private  subroutine oi_set_dense_enabled(this, enabled) Enables or disables explicit dense-output preparation.\nWhen enabled, the integrator prepares dense output for each accepted\nstep independently of whether the requested output grid requires it.\nDisabling this setting does not prevent dense output needed to produce\nrequested solution values. Any previously prepared step is invalidated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. logical, intent(in) :: enabled True to enable explicit dense-output preparation; false to disable it. procedure, public :: set_maximum_step_size => oi_set_max_step Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_max_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. procedure, public :: set_minimum_step_size => oi_set_min_step Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_min_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. generic, public :: set_relative_tolerance => oi_set_rel_tol, oi_set_rel_tols private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tol(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. re