bject. Return Value type( ode_results ) The ode_results container. procedure, public :: get_order => kc5_get_order Gets the order of the integrator. private pure function kc5_get_order(this) result(rst) Gets the order of the integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter_5 ), intent(in) :: this The kennedy_carpenter_5 object. Return Value integer The order. procedure, public :: get_relative_tolerance => oi_get_rel_tol Gets the relative error tolerance. private pure function oi_get_rel_tol(this, equation) result(rst) Gets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: equation The equation index. If omitted, the scalar tolerance is returned. Return Value real(kind=real64) The tolerance value. procedure, public :: get_solution => oi_get_solution Returns the solution computed by the integrator. private pure function oi_get_solution(this) result(rst) Returns the solution computed by the integrator stored as a matrix with\nthe first column containing the values of the independent variable at\nwhich the solution was computed.  The remaining columns contain the\nsolutions for each of the integrated equations in the order in which they\nappear in the source routine.  Notice, the solve routine must be called\nbefore this routine. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:,:) The resulting solution matrix. procedure, public :: get_stage_count => kc_get_stage_count Gets the stage count for this integrator. private pure function kc_get_stage_count(this) result(rst) Gets the stage count for this integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(in) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. Return Value integer The stage count. procedure, public :: get_step_limit => oi_get_step_limit Gets the limit on the number of integration steps. private pure function oi_get_step_limit(this) result(rst) Gets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value integer The step limit. procedure, public :: get_step_size_control_parameter => oi_get_control_parameter Gets the step size PI control parameter. private pure function oi_get_control_parameter(this) result(rst) Gets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The control parameter. procedure, public :: get_step_size_factor => oi_get_safety_factor Gets the step size safety factor. private pure function oi_get_safety_factor(this) result(rst) Gets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The safety factor. procedure, public :: has_dense_output => oi_has_dense_output Tests whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. private pure function oi_has_dense_output(this) result(rst) Determines whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. Return Value logical True if dense output is currently valid; otherwise, false. procedure, public :: interpolate => kc_interpolate Performs the interpolation. private  subroutine kc_interpolate(this, x, xn, yn, fn, xn1, yn1, fn1, y) Performs the interpolation. A cubic Hermite polynomial is constructed from the solution and\nderivative values at each end of the step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(in) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The value of the independent variable at which to compute\nthe interpolation. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn The previous value of the independent variable at which the\nsolution is computed. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array containing the solution at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn1 The value of the independent variable at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn1 An N-element array containing the solution at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn1 An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array where this routine will write the\nsolution values interpolated at x. procedure, public :: invalidate_dense_output => oi_invalidate_dense Invalidates the prepared interpolant before stepping or resetting. private  subroutine oi_invalidate_dense(this) Marks any prepared dense-output interpolant as unavailable. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. procedure, public :: log_failed_step => oi_log_failed_step Logs a failed integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_failed_step(this, n) Logs a failed integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: log_function_evaluation => oi_log_function_eval Logs a function evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_function_eval(this, n) Logs a function evaluation, or evaluations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one function \nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single \nfunction evaluation. procedure, public :: log_jacobian_evaluation => oi_log_jacobian_eval Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_jacobian_eval(this, n) Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one Jacobian matrix\nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nJacobian evaluation. procedure, public :: log_matrix_factorization => oi_log_matrix_factorization Logs a matrix factorization. private  subroutine oi_log_matrix_factorization(this, n) Logs a matrix factorization. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one matrix \nfactorization.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nfactorization. procedure, public :: log_successful_step => oi_log_successful_step Logs a successful integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_successful_step(this, n) Logs a successful integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: post_step_action => kc_post_step Performs any post-step actions. private  subroutine kc_post_step(this, sys, dense, x, xn, y, yn, f, fn, k, args) Retains the first-stage derivative for cubic Hermite interpolation. For a mass-matrix problem, the driver's f is a raw RHS rather than a\nderivative. The first stage supplies the consistent left-end slope;\nthe stiffly accurate final stage already supplies the right-end slope. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(inout) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. logical, intent(in) :: dense Determines if dense output is requested (true); else, false. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The previous value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array containing the solution at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the derivatives at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: k An N-by-NSTAGES matrix containing the derivatives at each stage. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: pre_step_action => kc_pre_step Performs any pre-step actions. private  subroutine kc_pre_step(this, prevs, sys, h, x, y, f, args) Marks the stored Jacobian as belonging to an earlier step once the\nsolution has advanced. The Jacobian itself is formed lazily by the step attempt, as it is only\nre-evaluated when the Newton iteration requires it. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(inout) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. logical, intent(in) :: prevs Defines the status of the previous step.  The value is true\nif the previous step was successful; else, false if the\nprevious step failed. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the current solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives\nat x. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. generic, public :: set_absolute_tolerance => oi_set_abs_tol, oi_set_abs_tols private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tol(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tols(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_allow_overshoot => oi_set_allow_overshoot Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. private  subroutine oi_set_allow_overshoot(this, x) Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot the final\nvalue in the integration range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. logical, intent(in) :: x True if the solver can overshoot, and then interpolate to achieve the\nrequired final value; else, false thereby indicating the solver \ncannot overshoot. procedure, public :: set_dense_interval => oi_set_dense_interval Implementation hook publishing a prepared accepted step. private  subroutine oi_set_dense_interval(this, x_start, x_end, n) Publishes the interval covered by retained dense-output interpolation\ndata for one accepted step. The endpoints are recorded in integration\norder, which may be increasing or decreasing. The interpolant is marked\nvalid after the interval and state dimension have been recorded.\nAn error stop occurs if either endpoint is non-finite, the endpoints\nare equal, or the state dimension is less than one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_start The first endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_end The second endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. integer, intent(in) :: n The number of dependent variables represented by the interpolant. procedure, public :: set_dense_output_enabled => oi_set_dense_enabled Enables dense output on every accepted step (default: false). private  subroutine oi_set_dense_enabled(this, enabled) Enables or disables explicit dense-output preparation.\nWhen enabled, the integrator prepares dense output for each accepted\nstep independently of whether the requested output grid requires it.\nDisabling this setting does not prevent dense output needed to produce\nrequested solution values. Any previously prepared step is invalidated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. logical, intent(in) :: enabled True to enable explicit dense-output preparation; false to disable it. procedure, public :: set_maximum_step_size => oi_set_max_step Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_max_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. procedure, public :: set_minimum_step_size => oi_set_min_step Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_min_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. procedure, public :: set_newton_step_limit => kc_set_newton_step_limit Sets the maximum number of Newton iterations allowed per stage. private  subroutine kc_set_newton_step_limit(this, x) Sets the maximum number of Newton iterations allowed per stage.  A\nvalue less than one causes DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(inout) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. integer, intent(in) :: x The iteration limit. procedure, public :: set_newton_tolerance => kc_set_newton_tolerance Sets the Newton iteration convergence tolerance. private  subroutine kc_set_newton_tolerance(this, x) Sets the convergence tolerance on the estimated Newton iteration error,\nrelative to the larger of one and the norm of the stage state.  The\ntolerance applied during integration is the lesser of this value and\none percent of the smallest positive integration tolerance.  A value\nthat is not positive and finite causes DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(inout) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The convergence tolerance. generic, public :: set_relative_tolerance => oi_set_rel_tol, oi_set_rel_tols private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tol(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tols(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_step_limit => oi_set_step_limit Sets the limit on the number of integration steps. private  subroutine oi_set_step_limit(this, x) Sets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: x The step limit. procedure, public :: set_step_size_control_parameter => oi_set_control_parameter Sets the step size PI control parameter. private  subroutine oi_set_control_parameter(this, x) Sets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The control parameter procedure, public :: set_step_size_factor => oi_set_safety_factor Sets the step size safety factor. private  subroutine oi_set_safety_factor(this, x) Sets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The safety factor. procedure, public :: solve => kc_solve private  subroutine kc_solve(this, sys, x, iv, store_iv, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( kennedy_carpenter ), intent(inout) :: this The kennedy_carpenter object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An array of independent variable values at which to return the \nthe solution to the ODE's. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: iv An array containing the initial values for each ODE. logical, intent(in), optional :: store_iv An optional input that determines whether or not the \ninitial values are stored as part of the output.  The\ndefault is true such that the initial values are stored;\nhowever, set to false to avoid storing the initial values.\nThis can be useful in cases of event detection where a \nrestart of the integrator is desired. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine.","tags":"","url":"type\\kennedy_carpenter_5.html"},{"title":"ode_results – DIFFEQ ","text":"type, public :: ode_results A container for ODE results. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ode_results_statistics ), public :: statistics Statistical information regarding the integration process. Constructor public        interface ode_results private pure function or_init_empty(n, capacity) result(rst) Initializes an empty ode_results container. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n The number of state variables.  A DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is\nthrown if this value is less than 1. integer, intent(in), optional :: capacity An optional input that sets the initial buffer capacity.  If \nsupplied, this value must be at least one or a \nDIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is thrown. Return Value type( ode_results ) The ode_results object. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: clear_all => or_clear_all private  subroutine or_clear_all(this) Clears the contents of this container, but does not alter its capacity.\nThe state variable count is reset; the next push sets the new count. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_results object. procedure, public :: count => or_get_count private pure function or_get_count(this) result(rst) Gets the number of solution points. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value integer The number of solution points. procedure, public :: get_capacity => or_get_capacity private pure function or_get_capacity(this) result(rst) Gets the current capacity of the container. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value integer The current capacity. procedure, public :: push => or_push_state private  subroutine or_push_state(this, x, y) Pushes a new state vector into the back of the container.\nThis is brand new.  Initialize the collection Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_results object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current state vector.  The dimensions of this vector must match\nthe value returned by state_variable_count(); else, a \nDIFFEQ_ARRAY_SIZE_ERROR will be thrown.  If the container is not\nyet initialized, the size of this vector will set the expected \nnumber of state variables.  The same applies after clear_all(). procedure, public :: selected_state => or_state_by_index private pure function or_state_by_index(this, index) result(rst) Gets the requested state variables by index.  If this routine is called\non an uninitialized container a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. integer, intent(in) :: index The one-based index for the state to return.  The index value must\nlie within the range [1, count()], else a DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR\nis thrown. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:) The state vector. procedure, public :: set_capacity => or_set_capacity private  subroutine or_set_capacity(this, n) Adjusts the capacity of the container.  If the container is not yet \ninitialized a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown.\nWhen shrinking below count(), only the first n solution points are kept. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_results object. integer, intent(in) :: n The new capacity.  This value must be at least one or a\nDIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is thrown. procedure, public :: solution_point => or_solution_point_by_index private pure function or_solution_point_by_index(this, index) result(rst) Gets the requested solution point by index.  If this routine is called\non an uninitialized container a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. integer, intent(in) :: index The one-based index for the state to return.  The index value must\nlie within the range [1, count()], else a DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR\nis thrown. Return Value real(kind=real64) The solution point. procedure, public :: solution_points => or_solution_points private pure function or_solution_points(this) result(rst) Gets a vector containing the independent variable values at which the\nsolution was computed.  If this routine is called on an uninitialized \ncontainer a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:) An M-element array where the solution points will be written.  M is \nequal to count(). generic, public :: state => or_whole_state, or_state_vector private pure function or_whole_state(this) result(rst) Gets the entire contents of the container.  If this routine is called\non an uninitialized container a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:,:) An M-by-N element matrix where the state variable values are \nreturned.  M is equal to count(), and N is equal to\nstate_variable_count(). private pure function or_state_vector(this, index) result(rst) Gets an entire state vector.   If this routine is called on an \nuninitialized container a DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. integer, intent(in) :: index The one-based index for the state vector to return.  The index value \nmust lie within the range [1, state_variable_count()], else a \nDIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is thrown. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:) An M-element array where the state vector will be returned.  M is \nequal to count(). procedure, public :: state_variable_count => or_get_state_count private pure function or_get_state_count(this) result(rst) Gets the number of state variables. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value integer The number of state variables. procedure, public :: to_matrix => or_to_matrix private pure function or_to_matrix(this) result(rst) Returns a copy of the contents of this container as a matrix with the \nfirst column containing the independent variable values at which the\nsolution was computed and the remaining columns containing the state\nvectors.  If this routine is called on an uninitialized container a \nDIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR is thrown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: this The ode_results object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:,:) The matrix.","tags":"","url":"type\\ode_results.html"},{"title":"ode_results_statistics – DIFFEQ ","text":"type, public :: ode_results_statistics A container of performance statistics for an\nintegrator. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: failed_steps = 0 The number of unsuccessful steps taken by the integrator. integer, public :: function_evaluations = 0 The number of RHS callback evaluations, including calls used for\nfinite differences, AD Jacobian columns, and time derivatives.\nExplicit Jacobian callbacks are counted separately; any RHS\ncalls made internally by user-owned Jacobian code are not tracked. integer, public :: jacobian_evaluations = 0 The number of Jacobian matrix evaluations. integer, public :: matrix_factorizations = 0 The number of matrix factorizations. integer, public :: successful_steps = 0 The number of successful steps taken by the integrator.","tags":"","url":"type\\ode_results_statistics.html"},{"title":"runge_kutta_853 – DIFFEQ ","text":"type, public, extends( single_step_integrator ) :: runge_kutta_853 The Fehlberg RK8(5,3) integrator. This method computes an eighth-order solution together with fifth-\nand third-order embedded solutions.  Its error estimate is , while the accepted\nsolution is the eighth-order result.  The higher order is useful\nfor smooth, non-stiff problems over long integration intervals. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ode_event_solver ), public :: event_solver The ODE event solver.  Enable event detection by defining the\nevent_function in the ode_container object. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: append_to_buffer => oi_append_to_buffer Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution \nbuffer. private  subroutine oi_append_to_buffer(this, x, y) Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution buffer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The independent variable value. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The values of the dependent variables corresponding to x. procedure, public :: attempt_step => rk853_attempt_step Attempts an integration step for this integrator. private  subroutine rk853_attempt_step(this, sys, h, x, y, f, yn, fn, yerr, k, args) Attempts an integration step for this integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(inout) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the current solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives\nat x. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nsolution estimate at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nderivative estimate at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: yerr An N-element array where this routine will write an estimate\nof the error in each equation. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: k An N-by-NSTAGES matrix containing the derivatives at each stage. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: clear_buffer => oi_clear_buffer Clears the contents of the buffer. private  subroutine oi_clear_buffer(this) Clears the contents of the buffer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. procedure, public :: compute_dense_output => ssi_dense_output private  subroutine ssi_dense_output(this, x, y) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( single_step_integrator ), intent(in) :: this real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: y (:) procedure, public :: compute_error_norm => rk853_estimate_error Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate. private pure function rk853_estimate_error(this, y, yest, yerr) result(rst) Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate.  A value less than one\nindicates a successful step.  A value greater than one suggests that the\nresults do not meet the requested tolerances. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(in) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The previously accepted solution array (N-element). real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(size(y)) :: yest An N-element array containing the next solution point estimate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(size(y)) :: yerr An N-element array containing the estimate of error for each\nequation. Return Value real(kind=real64) The norm of the scaled error. procedure, public :: estimate_inital_step_size => oi_initial_step Computes an estimate of an initial step size. private  subroutine oi_initial_step(this, sys, xo, xf, yo, fo, h, args) Computes an estimate of an initial step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xo The initial value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xf The final value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yo The initial values of the dependent variables (N-element). real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(size(yo)) :: fo An N-element array where the function values at xo will be written. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: h The initial step size estimate. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: estimate_next_step_size => oi_next_step Estimates the next step size. private  function oi_next_step(this, e, eold, h, x) result(rst) Estimates the next step size based upon the current and previous error\nestimates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: e The norm of the current scaled error estimate. real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: eold The norm of the previous step's scaled error estimate.  On output,\nthis variable is updated. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current independent variable value. Return Value real(kind=real64) The new step size estimate. procedure, public :: evaluate_dense => oi_evaluate_dense Evaluates the prepared step without advancing integration. private  subroutine oi_evaluate_dense(this, x, y) Evaluates the interpolant for the last prepared accepted step at a\nrequested independent-variable value. The query must be finite and\nwithin the step interval, including either endpoint. This operation\ndoes not advance or otherwise change solver state and does not evaluate\nthe ODE function. An error stop occurs if no valid interpolant is\navailable, the output array has the wrong size, or the query is\nnon-finite or outside the interval. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator containing the prepared interpolant. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The independent-variable value at which to evaluate the solution. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: y (:) Receives the interpolated dependent-variable values. Its size must\nequal the number of dependent variables in the prepared step. procedure, public :: get_absolute_tolerance => oi_get_abs_tol Gets the absolute error tolerance. private pure function oi_get_abs_tol(this, equation) result(rst) Gets the absolute error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: equation The equation index. If omitted, the scalar tolerance is returned. Return Value real(kind=real64) The tolerance value. procedure, public :: get_allow_overshoot => oi_get_allow_overshoot Gets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. private pure function oi_get_allow_overshoot(this) result(rst) Gets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot the final\nvalue in the integration range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value logical True if the solver can overshoot, and then interpolate to achieve the\nrequired final value; else, false thereby indicating the solver \ncannot overshoot. procedure, public :: get_dense_interval => oi_get_dense_interval Gets the prepared step's start and end in integration order. private  subroutine oi_get_dense_interval(this, x_start, x_end) Gets the endpoints of the currently prepared dense-output interval.\nAn error stop occurs if no valid interpolant is available. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: x_start Receives the first endpoint in integration order. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: x_end Receives the second endpoint in integration order. procedure, public :: get_dense_output_enabled => oi_get_dense_enabled Gets the explicit dense-output preparation setting. private pure function oi_get_dense_enabled(this) result(rst) Gets the explicit dense-output preparation setting. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. Return Value logical True if explicit dense-output preparation is enabled; otherwise,\nfalse. This setting is independent of preparation required to\nproduce values on a requested output grid. procedure, public :: get_is_fsal => rk853_get_is_fsal Gets a logical parameter stating if this is a first-same-as-last\n(FSAL) integrator. private pure function rk853_get_is_fsal(this) result(rst) Gets a logical parameter stating if this is a first-same-as-last\n(FSAL) integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(in) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. Return Value logical True for a FSAL integrator; else, false. procedure, public :: get_maximum_step_size => oi_get_max_step Gets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private pure function oi_get_max_step(this) result(rst) Gets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The step size limit. procedure, public :: get_minimum_step_size => oi_get_min_step Gets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private pure function oi_get_min_step(this) result(rst) Gets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The step size limit. procedure, public :: get_ode_results => oi_get_ode_results Returns the solution stored within an ode_results object. private pure function oi_get_ode_results(this) result(rst) Returns a copy of the solution computed as a ode_results container.\nThe integrator retains the original copy. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value type( ode_results ) The ode_results container. procedure, public :: get_order => rk853_get_order Gets the order of the integrator. private pure function rk853_get_order(this) result(rst) Gets the order of the integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(in) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. Return Value integer The order. procedure, public :: get_relative_tolerance => oi_get_rel_tol Gets the relative error tolerance. private pure function oi_get_rel_tol(this, equation) result(rst) Gets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: equation The equation index. If omitted, the scalar tolerance is returned. Return Value real(kind=real64) The tolerance value. procedure, public :: get_solution => oi_get_solution Returns the solution computed by the integrator. private pure function oi_get_solution(this) result(rst) Returns the solution computed by the integrator stored as a matrix with\nthe first column containing the values of the independent variable at\nwhich the solution was computed.  The remaining columns contain the\nsolutions for each of the integrated equations in the order in which they\nappear in the source routine.  Notice, the solve routine must be called\nbefore this routine. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:,:) The resulting solution matrix. procedure, public :: get_stage_count => rk853_get_stage_count Gets the stage count for this integrator. private pure function rk853_get_stage_count(this) result(rst) Gets the stage count for this integrator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(in) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. Return Value integer The stage count. procedure, public :: get_step_limit => oi_get_step_limit Gets the limit on the number of integration steps. private pure function oi_get_step_limit(this) result(rst) Gets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value integer The step limit. procedure, public :: get_step_size_control_parameter => oi_get_control_parameter Gets the step size PI control parameter. private pure function oi_get_control_parameter(this) result(rst) Gets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The control parameter. procedure, public :: get_step_size_factor => oi_get_safety_factor Gets the step size safety factor. private pure function oi_get_safety_factor(this) result(rst) Gets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The safety factor. procedure, public :: has_dense_output => oi_has_dense_output Tests whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. private pure function oi_has_dense_output(this) result(rst) Determines whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. Return Value logical True if dense output is currently valid; otherwise, false. procedure, public :: interpolate => rk853_interp Performs the interpolation. private  subroutine rk853_interp(this, x, xn, yn, fn, xn1, yn1, fn1, y) Performs the interpolation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(in) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The value of the independent variable at which to compute\nthe interpolation. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn The previous value of the independent variable at which the\nsolution is computed. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array containing the solution at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn1 The value of the independent variable at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn1 An N-element array containing the solution at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn1 An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array where this routine will write the \nsolution values interpolated at x. procedure, public :: invalidate_dense_output => oi_invalidate_dense Invalidates the prepared interpolant before stepping or resetting. private  subroutine oi_invalidate_dense(this) Marks any prepared dense-output interpolant as unavailable. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. procedure, public :: log_failed_step => oi_log_failed_step Logs a failed integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_failed_step(this, n) Logs a failed integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: log_function_evaluation => oi_log_function_eval Logs a function evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_function_eval(this, n) Logs a function evaluation, or evaluations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one function \nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single \nfunction evaluation. procedure, public :: log_jacobian_evaluation => oi_log_jacobian_eval Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_jacobian_eval(this, n) Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one Jacobian matrix\nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nJacobian evaluation. procedure, public :: log_matrix_factorization => oi_log_matrix_factorization Logs a matrix factorization. private  subroutine oi_log_matrix_factorization(this, n) Logs a matrix factorization. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one matrix \nfactorization.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nfactorization. procedure, public :: log_successful_step => oi_log_successful_step Logs a successful integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_successful_step(this, n) Logs a successful integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: post_step_action => rk853_set_up_interp Sets up the interpolation process as the post-step action. private  subroutine rk853_set_up_interp(this, sys, dense, x, xn, y, yn, f, fn, k, args) Sets up the interpolation process. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(inout) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. logical, intent(in) :: dense Determines if dense output is requested (true); else, false. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The previous value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xn The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array containing the solution at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the derivatives at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array containing the derivatives at xn. real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: k An N-by-NSTAGES matrix containing the derivatives at each stage. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: pre_step_action => rk853_pre_step Performs any pre-step actions. Initializes private storage arrays for the integrator. private  subroutine rk853_pre_step(this, prevs, sys, h, x, y, f, args) Placeholder routine for any pre-step actions. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( runge_kutta_853 ), intent(inout) :: this The runge_kutta_853 object. logical, intent(in) :: prevs Defines the status of the previous step.  The value is true \nif the previous step was successful; else, false if the \nprevious step failed. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the current solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives\nat x. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. generic, public :: set_absolute_tolerance => oi_set_abs_tol, oi_set_abs_tols private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tol(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tols(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_allow_overshoot => oi_set_allow_overshoot Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. private  subroutine oi_set_allow_overshoot(this, x) Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot the final\nvalue in the integration range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. logical, intent(in) :: x True if the solver can overshoot, and then interpolate to achieve the\nrequired final value; else, false thereby indicating the solver \ncannot overshoot. procedure, public :: set_dense_interval => oi_set_dense_interval Implementation hook publishing a prepared accepted step. private  subroutine oi_set_dense_interval(this, x_start, x_end, n) Publishes the interval covered by retained dense-output interpolation\ndata for one accepted step. The endpoints are recorded in integration\norder, which may be increasing or decreasing. The interpolant is marked\nvalid after the interval and state dimension have been recorded.\nAn error stop occurs if either endpoint is non-finite, the endpoints\nare equal, or the state dimension is less than one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_start The first endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_end The second endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. integer, intent(in) :: n The number of dependent variables represented by the interpolant. procedure, public :: set_dense_output_enabled => oi_set_dense_enabled Enables dense output on every accepted step (default: false). private  subroutine oi_set_dense_enabled(this, enabled) Enables or disables explicit dense-output preparation.\nWhen enabled, the integrator prepares dense output for each accepted\nstep independently of whether the requested output grid requires it.\nDisabling this setting does not prevent dense output needed to produce\nrequested solution values. Any previously prepared step is invalidated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. logical, intent(in) :: enabled True to enable explicit dense-output preparation; false to disable it. procedure, public :: set_maximum_step_size => oi_set_max_step Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_max_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. procedure, public :: set_minimum_step_size => oi_set_min_step Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_min_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. generic, public :: set_relative_tolerance => oi_set_rel_tol, oi_set_rel_tols private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tol(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tols(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_step_limit => oi_set_step_limit Sets the limit on the number of integration steps. private  subroutine oi_set_step_limit(this, x) Sets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: x The step limit. procedure, public :: set_step_size_control_parameter => oi_set_control_parameter Sets the step size PI control parameter. private  subroutine oi_set_control_parameter(this, x) Sets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The control parameter procedure, public :: set_step_size_factor => oi_set_safety_factor Sets the step size safety factor. private  subroutine oi_set_safety_factor(this, x) Sets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The safety factor. procedure, public :: solve => ssi_ode_solver Solves the supplied system of ODE's. public  subroutine ssi_ode_solver (this, sys, x, iv, store_iv, args) Solves the supplied system of ODE's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( single_step_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The single_step_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An array of independent variable values at which to return the \nthe solution to the ODE's. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: iv An array containing the initial values for each ODE. logical, intent(in), optional :: store_iv An optional input that determines whether or not the \ninitial values are stored as part of the output.  The\ndefault is true such that the initial values are stored;\nhowever, set to false to avoid storing the initial values.\nThis can be useful in cases of event detection where a \nrestart of the integrator is desired. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine.","tags":"","url":"type\\runge_kutta_853.html"},{"title":"c_ggl_container – DIFFEQ ","text":"type, public, bind(C) :: c_ggl_container C-interoperable description of a holonomically constrained\nmechanical model to be solved with the stabilized index-1\nGear-Gupta-Leimkuhler (GGL) formulation of ggl_container . For N coordinates and M constraints the integrated state is so the state count supplied to the DAE integrators must equal , and the initial conditions must use this ordering.\nThe model is where are the position constraints and . Every callback must accept perturbed,\noff-manifold states, and the constraint callbacks must not depend\non the independent variable. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=c_double), public :: alpha = 0.0d0 Nonnegative, finite position-constraint decay rate, in inverse\nindependent-variable units. Zero disables position damping. real(kind=c_double), public :: beta = 0.0d0 Nonnegative, finite velocity-constraint decay rate, in inverse\nindependent-variable units. Zero disables velocity damping. integer(kind=c_int), public :: constraint_count = 0 The number M of independent constraints, with . type(c_funptr), public :: constraints Required c_dae_algebraic_constraints callback receiving\nthe N-element coordinate vector q and writing the M position\nconstraint residuals . type(c_funptr), public :: curvature Required c_dae_constraint_curvature callback computing the\nM curvature terms . Return zeros for linear\nconstraints. integer(kind=c_int), public :: event_equation_count = 0 The number of event equations in events. type(c_funptr), public :: events Optional c_ode_event_function for enabling event detection.\nTo fully enable event detection, event_equation_count must be\ngreater than zero as well. type(c_funptr), public :: force Required c_ode callback computing the applied force , excluding multiplier forces. It is called with\nn = 2N and receives the 2N-element vector [q, v], but must\nwrite only the N-element force vector. type(c_funptr), public :: gradient Required c_ode_jacobian callback receiving the N-element\ncoordinate vector q and writing the M-by-N constraint\nJacobian in column-major order.\nThe rows of must be linearly independent. type(c_funptr), public :: jacobian Optional callback for computing the Jacobian matrix of the \ncomplete system, including the constraints.  If not supplied, \nthe Jacobian will be estimated with finite differences. type(c_funptr), public :: mass Optional c_ode_mass_matrix callback receiving the\nN-element coordinate vector q and writing the N-by-N\nsymmetric positive-definite physical mass matrix. Set to\nC_NULL_FUNPTR to use the identity matrix. Set the\nmass_matrix_constant setting to false whenever this matrix\nvaries with x or q.","tags":"","url":"type\\c_ggl_container.html"},{"title":"adams – DIFFEQ ","text":"type, public, extends( multistep_integrator ) :: adams A variable step-size, variable order (1-12) Adams-Bashforth-Moulton\nintegrator operating in predictor-corrector (PECE) mode. The corrector is applied once rather than iterated to convergence,\nwhich is what distinguishes PECE from a fully implicit method.  A\nsingle correction is only contractive while , where bounds the Lipschitz constant of the problem, so this\nintegrator is intended for non-stiff systems.  Applied to a stiff\nproblem it holds its accuracy only by driving the step size down to\nwhat stability permits, which can cost orders of magnitude more\nsteps than an implicit method requires; such a problem belongs to\nbdf or to one of the implicit Runge-Kutta integrators. A system carrying a mass matrix is supported, but the matrix must be\nnonsingular.  The method needs itself, so the mass matrix is\nfactored and resolved rather than merely appearing as a factor, and\na singular matrix is reported as an error.  A differential-algebraic\nproblem must therefore be given to bdf. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ode_event_solver ), public :: event_solver The ODE event solver.  Enable event detection by defining the\nevent_function in the ode_container object. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: append_to_buffer => oi_append_to_buffer Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution \nbuffer. private  subroutine oi_append_to_buffer(this, x, y) Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution buffer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The independent variable value. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The values of the dependent variables corresponding to x. procedure, public :: clear_buffer => oi_clear_buffer Clears the contents of the buffer. private  subroutine oi_clear_buffer(this) Clears the contents of the buffer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. procedure, public :: compute_dense_output => mi_dense_output private  subroutine mi_dense_output(this, x, y) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: y (:) procedure, public :: compute_error_norm => oi_estimate_error Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate. private pure function oi_estimate_error(this, y, yest, yerr) result(rst) Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate.  A value less than one\nindicates a successful step.  A value greater than one suggests that the\nresults do not meet the requested tolerances. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The previously accepted solution array (N-element). real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(size(y)) :: yest An N-element array containing the next solution point estimate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(size(y)) :: yerr An N-element array containing the estimate of error for each\nequation. Return Value real(kind=real64) The norm of the scaled error. procedure, public :: correct => adams_correct Applies the Adams-Moulton corrector. private  subroutine adams_correct(this, sys, h, x, ypred, ynew, converged, args) Applies the Adams-Moulton corrector. The corrector repeats the integration with the derivative at the new\npoint included among the interpolation nodes, raising the degree of the\nfitted polynomial by one over the predictor at no additional cost, as\nthat derivative was already evaluated.  It is applied exactly once; a\nstep for which one correction does not suffice is rejected by the error\ntest and retried on a shorter step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(inout) :: this The adams object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: ypred The N-element array containing the predicted values at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: ynew The new estimate of the dependent variables. logical, intent(out) :: converged True if the corrector succeeded; else, false. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information in and out\nof the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: estimate_inital_step_size => oi_initial_step Computes an estimate of an initial step size. private  subroutine oi_initial_step(this, sys, xo, xf, yo, fo, h, args) Computes an estimate of an initial step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xo The initial value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xf The final value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: yo The initial values of the dependent variables (N-element). real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(size(yo)) :: fo An N-element array where the function values at xo will be written. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: h The initial step size estimate. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: estimate_next_step_size => oi_next_step Estimates the next step size. private  function oi_next_step(this, e, eold, h, x) result(rst) Estimates the next step size based upon the current and previous error\nestimates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: e The norm of the current scaled error estimate. real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: eold The norm of the previous step's scaled error estimate.  On output,\nthis variable is updated. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current independent variable value. Return Value real(kind=real64) The new step size estimate. procedure, public :: evaluate_dense => oi_evaluate_dense Evaluates the prepared step without advancing integration. private  subroutine oi_evaluate_dense(this, x, y) Evaluates the interpolant for the last prepared accepted step at a\nrequested independent-variable value. The query must be finite and\nwithin the step interval, including either endpoint. This operation\ndoes not advance or otherwise change solver state and does not evaluate\nthe ODE function. An error stop occurs if no valid interpolant is\navailable, the output array has the wrong size, or the query is\nnon-finite or outside the interval. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator containing the prepared interpolant. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The independent-variable value at which to evaluate the solution. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: y (:) Receives the interpolated dependent-variable values. Its size must\nequal the number of dependent variables in the prepared step. procedure, public :: evaluate_derivative => adams_evaluate_derivative Evaluates the derivative, resolving any mass matrix. private  subroutine adams_evaluate_derivative(this, sys, x, y, dydx, args) Evaluates the derivative, resolving any mass matrix. An Adams method integrates the derivative itself, so a system written as requires that the mass matrix be resolved rather than\nsimply carried along.  The matrix is factored once and reused for as\nlong as it remains valid, and a factorization that proves to be singular\nis reported rather than resolved in some least-squares sense, since a\nsingular mass matrix places the problem beyond what this method can\nrepresent. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(inout) :: this The adams object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array containing the solution at x. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: dydx An N-element array where the derivative will be written. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information in and out\nof the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: get_absolute_tolerance => oi_get_abs_tol Gets the absolute error tolerance. private pure function oi_get_abs_tol(this, equation) result(rst) Gets the absolute error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: equation The equation index. If omitted, the scalar tolerance is returned. Return Value real(kind=real64) The tolerance value. procedure, public :: get_allow_overshoot => oi_get_allow_overshoot Gets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. private pure function oi_get_allow_overshoot(this) result(rst) Gets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot the final\nvalue in the integration range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value logical True if the solver can overshoot, and then interpolate to achieve the\nrequired final value; else, false thereby indicating the solver \ncannot overshoot. procedure, public :: get_dense_interval => oi_get_dense_interval Gets the prepared step's start and end in integration order. private  subroutine oi_get_dense_interval(this, x_start, x_end) Gets the endpoints of the currently prepared dense-output interval.\nAn error stop occurs if no valid interpolant is available. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: x_start Receives the first endpoint in integration order. real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: x_end Receives the second endpoint in integration order. procedure, public :: get_dense_output_enabled => oi_get_dense_enabled Gets the explicit dense-output preparation setting. private pure function oi_get_dense_enabled(this) result(rst) Gets the explicit dense-output preparation setting. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. Return Value logical True if explicit dense-output preparation is enabled; otherwise,\nfalse. This setting is independent of preparation required to\nproduce values on a requested output grid. procedure, public :: get_error_constant => adams_error_constant Gets the error constant for the requested order. private pure function adams_error_constant(this, k) result(rst) Gets the constant relating the difference between the corrected and\npredicted solutions to the local truncation error of the formula. Writing the errors of the two formulae as and , their difference eliminates the derivative\nand leaves the corrector error as .  This is the Milne\ndevice, and the values returned here are those ratios. In terms of the Adams coefficients the ratio is , the denominator following\nfrom . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(in) :: this The adams object. integer, intent(in) :: k The order of interest. Return Value real(kind=real64) The error constant. procedure, public :: get_maximum_order => mi_get_max_order Gets the upper limit on the order of the method. private pure function mi_get_max_order(this) result(rst) Gets the upper limit on the order of the method. The value reported is the limit actually in force, which is the lesser\nof any limit requested by the caller and the highest order the method\nsupports. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. Return Value integer The order limit. procedure, public :: get_maximum_step_size => oi_get_max_step Gets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private pure function oi_get_max_step(this) result(rst) Gets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The step size limit. procedure, public :: get_maximum_supported_order => adams_max_order Gets the highest order the method is permitted to use. private pure function adams_max_order(this) result(rst) Gets the highest order this integrator is permitted to use. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(in) :: this The adams object. Return Value integer The order limit. procedure, public :: get_minimum_step_size => oi_get_min_step Gets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private pure function oi_get_min_step(this) result(rst) Gets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The step size limit. procedure, public :: get_ode_results => oi_get_ode_results Returns the solution stored within an ode_results object. private pure function oi_get_ode_results(this) result(rst) Returns a copy of the solution computed as a ode_results container.\nThe integrator retains the original copy. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value type( ode_results ) The ode_results container. procedure, public :: get_order => mi_get_order Gets the order currently in use. private pure function mi_get_order(this) result(rst) Gets the order of the integrator currently in use. A variable-order method changes this value as the integration proceeds,\nso it reports the order of the most recently attempted step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. Return Value integer The order. procedure, public :: get_relative_tolerance => oi_get_rel_tol Gets the relative error tolerance. private pure function oi_get_rel_tol(this, equation) result(rst) Gets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: equation The equation index. If omitted, the scalar tolerance is returned. Return Value real(kind=real64) The tolerance value. procedure, public :: get_solution => oi_get_solution Returns the solution computed by the integrator. private pure function oi_get_solution(this) result(rst) Returns the solution computed by the integrator stored as a matrix with\nthe first column containing the values of the independent variable at\nwhich the solution was computed.  The remaining columns contain the\nsolutions for each of the integrated equations in the order in which they\nappear in the source routine.  Notice, the solve routine must be called\nbefore this routine. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:,:) The resulting solution matrix. procedure, public :: get_step_limit => oi_get_step_limit Gets the limit on the number of integration steps. private pure function oi_get_step_limit(this) result(rst) Gets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value integer The step limit. procedure, public :: get_step_size_control_parameter => oi_get_control_parameter Gets the step size PI control parameter. private pure function oi_get_control_parameter(this) result(rst) Gets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The control parameter. procedure, public :: get_step_size_factor => oi_get_safety_factor Gets the step size safety factor. private pure function oi_get_safety_factor(this) result(rst) Gets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value real(kind=real64) The safety factor. procedure, public :: get_stored_derivative => mi_get_stored_f Gets a stored derivative vector. private pure function mi_get_stored_f(this, i) result(rst) Gets a stored derivative vector, where an index of one denotes the most\nrecently accepted point. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: i The one-based index into the history. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:) The stored derivative. procedure, public :: get_stored_solution => mi_get_stored_y Gets a stored solution vector. private pure function mi_get_stored_y(this, i) result(rst) Gets a stored solution vector, where an index of one denotes the most\nrecently accepted point. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: i The one-based index into the history. Return Value real(kind=real64), allocatable, dimension(:) The stored solution. procedure, public :: get_stored_step_count => mi_get_stored_count Gets the number of solution points held in the history. private pure function mi_get_stored_count(this) result(rst) Gets the number of previously accepted solution points currently held in\nthe history. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. Return Value integer The number of stored points. procedure, public :: get_stored_variable => mi_get_stored_x Gets a stored independent variable value. private pure function mi_get_stored_x(this, i) result(rst) Gets a stored value of the independent variable, where an index of one\ndenotes the most recently accepted point. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: i The one-based index into the history. Return Value real(kind=real64) The stored value. procedure, public :: get_truncation_constant => adams_truncation_constant Gets the truncation error constant for the requested order. private pure function adams_truncation_constant(this, k) result(rst) Gets the constant relating the -th difference of the solution\nto the local truncation error of the corrector. These are the error constants of the Adams-Moulton formulae themselves,\nwritten , and they differ from those returned by\nget_error_constant because the Adams predictor is not an extrapolation\nof the solution history. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(in) :: this The adams object. integer, intent(in) :: k The order of interest. Return Value real(kind=real64) The truncation error constant. procedure, public :: has_dense_output => oi_has_dense_output Tests whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. private pure function oi_has_dense_output(this) result(rst) Determines whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ODE integrator. Return Value logical True if dense output is currently valid; otherwise, false. procedure, public :: interpolate => mi_interpolate Interpolates the solution history to the requested point. private  subroutine mi_interpolate(this, x, y) Interpolates the stored solution history to the requested value of the\nindependent variable. The polynomial passing through the most recently accepted points is the\nsame polynomial on which the method itself is based, so dense output\ncarries the accuracy of the current order and costs no additional\nfunction evaluations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The value of the independent variable at which to compute the\ninterpolation. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array where the interpolated solution is written. procedure, public :: invalidate_dense_output => oi_invalidate_dense Invalidates the prepared interpolant before stepping or resetting. private  subroutine oi_invalidate_dense(this) Marks any prepared dense-output interpolant as unavailable. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. procedure, public :: log_failed_step => oi_log_failed_step Logs a failed integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_failed_step(this, n) Logs a failed integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: log_function_evaluation => oi_log_function_eval Logs a function evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_function_eval(this, n) Logs a function evaluation, or evaluations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one function \nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single \nfunction evaluation. procedure, public :: log_jacobian_evaluation => oi_log_jacobian_eval Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. private  subroutine oi_log_jacobian_eval(this, n) Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one Jacobian matrix\nevaluation.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nJacobian evaluation. procedure, public :: log_matrix_factorization => oi_log_matrix_factorization Logs a matrix factorization. private  subroutine oi_log_matrix_factorization(this, n) Logs a matrix factorization. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one matrix \nfactorization.  If not supplied, this routine will log a single\nfactorization. procedure, public :: log_successful_step => oi_log_successful_step Logs a successful integration step. private  subroutine oi_log_successful_step(this, n) Logs a successful integration step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in), optional :: n An optional input useful for logging more than one step.  If not\nsupplied, this routine will log a single step. procedure, public :: predictor => adams_predictor Evaluates the Adams-Bashforth predictor. private  subroutine adams_predictor(this, sys, h, x, y, f, yn, fn, args) Evaluates the Adams-Bashforth predictor. The predictor integrates the polynomial fitted to the k most recent\nderivatives across the step.  The derivative is then evaluated at the\npredicted solution, which is the first evaluation of the PECE cycle and\nis retained for the corrector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(inout) :: this The adams object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current value(s) of the dependent variable(s). real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives at x. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array where this routine will write the next solution\nestimate at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nderivative estimate at x + h. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information in and out\nof the differential equation subroutine. procedure, public :: prepare_for_solve => adams_prepare_for_solve Discards the cached mass matrix factorization. private  subroutine adams_prepare_for_solve(this) Discards the cached mass matrix factorization. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( adams ), intent(inout) :: this The adams object. procedure, public :: reset_history => mi_reset_history Clears the stored solution history. private  subroutine mi_reset_history(this) Clears the stored solution history. The integrator restarts at first order the next time it is used. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. generic, public :: set_absolute_tolerance => oi_set_abs_tol, oi_set_abs_tols private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tol(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_abs_tols(this, x) Sets the absolute error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_allow_overshoot => oi_set_allow_overshoot Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. private  subroutine oi_set_allow_overshoot(this, x) Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot the final\nvalue in the integration range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. logical, intent(in) :: x True if the solver can overshoot, and then interpolate to achieve the\nrequired final value; else, false thereby indicating the solver \ncannot overshoot. procedure, public :: set_dense_interval => oi_set_dense_interval Implementation hook publishing a prepared accepted step. private  subroutine oi_set_dense_interval(this, x_start, x_end, n) Publishes the interval covered by retained dense-output interpolation\ndata for one accepted step. The endpoints are recorded in integration\norder, which may be increasing or decreasing. The interpolant is marked\nvalid after the interval and state dimension have been recorded.\nAn error stop occurs if either endpoint is non-finite, the endpoints\nare equal, or the state dimension is less than one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_start The first endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x_end The second endpoint of the accepted step in integration order. integer, intent(in) :: n The number of dependent variables represented by the interpolant. procedure, public :: set_dense_output_enabled => oi_set_dense_enabled Enables dense output on every accepted step (default: false). private  subroutine oi_set_dense_enabled(this, enabled) Enables or disables explicit dense-output preparation.\nWhen enabled, the integrator prepares dense output for each accepted\nstep independently of whether the requested output grid requires it.\nDisabling this setting does not prevent dense output needed to produce\nrequested solution values. Any previously prepared step is invalidated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ODE integrator. logical, intent(in) :: enabled True to enable explicit dense-output preparation; false to disable it. procedure, public :: set_maximum_order => mi_set_max_order Sets the upper limit on the order of the method. private  subroutine mi_set_max_order(this, x) Sets the upper limit on the order of the method. The value is constrained to the range supported by the method. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: x The order limit. procedure, public :: set_maximum_step_size => oi_set_max_step Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_max_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. procedure, public :: set_minimum_step_size => oi_set_min_step Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. private  subroutine oi_set_min_step(this, x) Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The step size limit. generic, public :: set_relative_tolerance => oi_set_rel_tol, oi_set_rel_tols private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tol(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The tolerance value. private  subroutine oi_set_rel_tols(this, x) Sets the relative error tolerance for each equation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x The tolerance values. procedure, public :: set_step_limit => oi_set_step_limit Sets the limit on the number of integration steps. private  subroutine oi_set_step_limit(this, x) Sets the limit on the number of integration steps that may be taken \nbefore the solver terminates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: x The step limit. procedure, public :: set_step_size_control_parameter => oi_set_control_parameter Sets the step size PI control parameter. private  subroutine oi_set_control_parameter(this, x) Sets the step size control parameter used for PI control of \nthe step size.  A value of 0 provides a default step size controller\n(non-PI); however, a nonzero value of provides PI control \nthat improves stability, but comes with a potential for efficiency loss.\nA good estimate for a starting point for this parameter is where is the order of the integrator. The PI controller for step size is defined as follows. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The control parameter procedure, public :: set_step_size_factor => oi_set_safety_factor Sets the step size safety factor. private  subroutine oi_set_safety_factor(this, x) Sets the safety factor (step size multiplier) used to provide a measure\nof control to the step size estimate such that ,\nwhere is this safety factor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The safety factor. procedure, public :: solve => mi_ode_solver Solves the supplied system of ODE's. private  subroutine mi_ode_solver(this, sys, x, iv, store_iv, args) Solves the supplied system of ODE's. The integration is driven by a predictor-corrector cycle.  Each step\nextrapolates the solution history to form a prediction, refines that\nprediction with Newton iteration on the implicit formula, and compares\nthe two to estimate the local error.  A step whose error satisfies the\nrequested tolerances is accepted and appended to the history; otherwise\nit is retried on a shorter step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An array of independent variable values at which to return the\nsolution to the ODE's.  If only two values are supplied, the\nsolution is returned at every successful integration step. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: iv An array containing the initial values for each ODE. logical, intent(in), optional :: store_iv An optional input that determines whether or not the \ninitial values are stored as part of the output.  The\ndefault is true such that the initial values are stored;\nhowever, set to false to avoid storing the initial values.\nThis can be useful in cases of event detection where a \nrestart of the integrator is desired. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine.","tags":"","url":"type\\adams.html"},{"title":"dae_algebraic_constraints – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine dae_algebraic_constraints(x, y, g, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The independent-variable value at which to evaluate the\nconstraints, normally time. Autonomous constraints may\nignore this argument. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y An N-element input state in the ordering defined by the\nmodel. No particular coordinate, velocity, or multiplier\npartition is imposed by this interface. It must not be\nmodified by the callback. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: g An M-element output array receiving the constraint\nresiduals in the model's declared constraint order.\nEvery element must be assigned on every call; incoming\ncontents are undefined. Exact constraint satisfaction\ncorresponds to a zero vector. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args Optional user-owned model parameters or evaluation state.\nCheck presence and dynamic type before accessing it.\nThe callback may update this object, but repeated calls\nwith the same inputs should give the same residuals unless\nthe user intentionally changes model parameters. This\nargument is not reserved for index-reduction workspace. Description Evaluates algebraic constraint residuals . For input state components and constraints,\nthe callback represents a mapping A consistent state satisfies . Return the\nresiduals themselves, not their derivatives, a Boolean result,\nor a projected state. A nonzero residual is a valid evaluation\nat an inconsistent state, rather than a callback failure. The caller supplies the input and output array sizes. The\nimplementation must interpret the same state ordering as its\nmodel and write every output element. This interface performs\nno dimension, rank, or initial-consistency checks. Residual\nordering and physical units are defined by the model; any\nsubsequent consistency tolerance must respect that scaling.","tags":"","url":"interface\\dae_algebraic_constraints.html"},{"title":"dae_constraint_curvature – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine dae_constraint_curvature(x, q, direction, v, curvature, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x Independent-variable value, provided for callback uniformity;\nautonomous constraints must not depend on it. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: q N coordinates, in the same order as the force model. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: direction N components of the coordinate derivative ,\nincluding the kinematic multiplier correction. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v N physical velocity components; these need not equal direction. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: curvature M curvature terms in the order of the constraint callback. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args Optional user-owned parameters, forwarded unchanged. Description Evaluates , without including . Each component is .\nAssign every output element. For linear constraints return\nzeros. The callback must support off-manifold coordinates and\narbitrary directions used during nonlinear/Jacobian evaluation.","tags":"","url":"interface\\dae_constraint_curvature.html"},{"title":"ode_dense_output – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine ode_dense_output(this, x, y) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: y (:)","tags":"","url":"interface\\ode_dense_output.html"},{"title":"ode_integer_inquiry – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public pure function ode_integer_inquiry(this) result(rst) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The ode_integrator object. Return Value integer The requested value. Description Returns an integer value from the ode_integrator object.","tags":"","url":"interface\\ode_integer_inquiry.html"},{"title":"ode_solver – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine ode_solver(this, sys, x, iv, store_iv, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ode_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The ode_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An array, of at least 2 values, defining at a minimum\nthe starting and ending values of the independent variable \nintegration range.  If more than two values are specified, \nthe integration results will be returned at the supplied \nvalues. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: iv An array containing the initial values for each ODE. logical, intent(in), optional :: store_iv An optional input that determines whether or not the \ninitial values are stored as part of the output.  The\ndefault is true such that the initial values are stored;\nhowever, set to false to avoid storing the initial values.\nThis can be useful in cases of event detection where a \nrestart of the integrator is desired. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. Description Solves the supplied system of ODE's.","tags":"","url":"interface\\ode_solver.html"},{"title":"c_dae_algebraic_constraints – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_dae_algebraic_constraints(nconstraints, nstates, x, y, g) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nconstraints The number of constraint equations. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state variables. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: y (nstates) The current state vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: g (nconstraints) The constraint vector. Description Evaluates algebraic constraint residuals . For input state components and constraints,\nthe callback represents a mapping A consistent state satisfies . Return the\nresiduals themselves, not their derivatives, a Boolean result,\nor a projected state. A nonzero residual is a valid evaluation\nat an inconsistent state, rather than a callback failure. The caller supplies the input and output array sizes. The\nimplementation must interpret the same state ordering as its\nmodel and write every output element. This interface performs\nno dimension, rank, or initial-consistency checks. Residual\nordering and physical units are defined by the model; any\nsubsequent consistency tolerance must respect that scaling.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_dae_algebraic_constraints.html"},{"title":"c_dae_constraint_curvature – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_dae_constraint_curvature(nconstraints, ncoord, x, q, direction, v, curvature) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nconstraints The number of constraint equations. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: ncoord The number of coordinate variables. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: q (ncoord) The current coordinate vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: direction (ncoord) The coordinate derivative , including the \nkinematic multiplier correction. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: v (ncoord) The physical velocity components. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: curvature (nconstraints) The curvature terms in the order of teh constraint callback. Description Evaluates , without including . Each component is .\nAssign every output element. For linear constraints return\nzeros. The callback must support off-manifold coordinates and\narbitrary directions used during nonlinear/Jacobian evaluation.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_dae_constraint_curvature.html"},{"title":"c_ode – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_ode(n, x, y, dydx) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: n The number of state variables. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: y (n) The current state vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: dydx (n) The state vector derivatives. Description ODE callback routine.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_ode.html"},{"title":"c_ode_event_function – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_ode_event_function(neqn, nstates, x, y, f) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: neqn The number of event equations. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: y (nstates) The current state vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: f (neqn) The event function values. Description Evaluates event functions for ODE event detection.  The solver\nseeks to locate roots for each equation.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_ode_event_function.html"},{"title":"c_ode_jacobian – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_ode_jacobian(m, n, x, y, jac, ldj) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: m The number of equations. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: n The state vector length. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: y (n) The current state vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: jac (ldj,n) The M-by-N Jacobian matrix. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: ldj The leading dimension of the Jacobian matrix. Description ODE Jacobian callback routine.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_ode_jacobian.html"},{"title":"c_ode_mass_matrix – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine c_ode_mass_matrix(n, x, y, m, ldm) bind(C) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: n The number of state variables. real(kind=c_double), intent(in), value :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: y (n) The current state vector. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: m (ldm,n) The mass matrix. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: ldm The leading dimension of the mass matrix. Description ODE mass matrix callback routine.","tags":"","url":"interface\\c_ode_mass_matrix.html"},{"title":"abs – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface abs Absolute value; the derivative at zero is defined to be zero. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_abs(a) result(c) Propagate sign(a)*da, choosing derivative zero at a = 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\abs.html"},{"title":"acos – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface acos Inverse cosine in radians; the active derivative is singular at +/-1. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_acos(a) result(c) Propagate -da/sqrt(1-a**2) using the inverse-sine derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\acos.html"},{"title":"acosh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface acosh Inverse hyperbolic cosine for values >= 1; active derivative singular at 1. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_acosh(a) result(c) Propagate da/(sqrt(a-1)*sqrt(a+1)); inactive seeds stay zero at a = 1. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\acosh.html"},{"title":"asin – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface asin Inverse sine in radians; the active derivative is singular at +/-1. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_asin(a) result(c) Propagate da/sqrt(1-a**2), omitting the singular term for inactive seeds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\asin.html"},{"title":"asinh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface asinh Inverse hyperbolic sine. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_asinh(a) result(c) Propagate da/sqrt(a**2+1), using HYPOT to avoid overflow. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\asinh.html"},{"title":"assignment(=) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface assignment(=) Copy AD data, assign a constant (clearing dx), or extract a real value. Module Procedures private elemental subroutine ad_assign_1(lhs, rhs) Copy the value and derivative of rhs to lhs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_2(lhs, rhs) Assign a real64 constant rhs to lhs and clear its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_3(lhs, rhs) Extract the value of rhs into real64 lhs, discarding the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: lhs type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_integer(lhs, rhs) Assign a default-integer constant rhs to lhs and clear its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs integer, intent(in) :: rhs","tags":"","url":"interface\\assignment(=).html"},{"title":"atan – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface atan One- or two-argument inverse tangent in radians. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_atan(a) result(c) Propagate da/(1+a**2), using HYPOT to avoid squaring large a. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2(y, x) result(c) Propagate (x dy-y dx)/(x 2+y 2) using a scaled radius. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2_real(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with AD ordinate y and constant abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_atan2_ad(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with constant ordinate y and AD abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\atan.html"},{"title":"atan2 – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface atan2 Quadrant-aware inverse tangent ATAN2(y,x); not defined at the origin. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_atan2(y, x) result(c) Propagate (x dy-y dx)/(x 2+y 2) using a scaled radius. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2_real(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with AD ordinate y and constant abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_atan2_ad(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with constant ordinate y and AD abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\atan2.html"},{"title":"atanh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface atanh Inverse hyperbolic tangent for values strictly between -1 and 1. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_atanh(a) result(c) Propagate da/(1-a**2) using factored divisions. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\atanh.html"},{"title":"cos – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface cos Cosine, with arguments in radians. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_cos(a) result(c) Propagate -sin(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\cos.html"},{"title":"cosh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface cosh Hyperbolic cosine. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_cosh(a) result(c) Propagate sinh(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\cosh.html"},{"title":"erf – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface erf Error function. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_erf(a) result(c) Propagate 2/sqrt(pi) exp(-a 2) da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\erf.html"},{"title":"erfc – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface erfc Complementary error function. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_erfc(a) result(c) Negate the error-function derivative for the complementary error function. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\erfc.html"},{"title":"exp – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface exp Natural exponential. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_exp(a) result(c) Propagate exp(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\exp.html"},{"title":"log – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface log Natural logarithm for positive values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_log(a) result(c) Propagate da/a for the natural logarithm. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\log.html"},{"title":"log10 – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface log10 Base-ten logarithm for positive values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_log10(a) result(c) Propagate da/(a*log(10)) for the base-ten logarithm. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\log10.html"},{"title":"max – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface max Binary maximum, carrying the selected derivative; first argument wins ties. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_max(a, b) result(c) Return the higher-valued operand with its derivative, choosing a on a tie. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_max_real(a, b) result(c) Select the maximum of AD a and constant b; selecting b clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_max_ad(a, b) result(c) Select the maximum of constant a and AD b; selecting a clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\max.html"},{"title":"min – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface min Binary minimum, carrying the selected derivative; first argument wins ties. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_min(a, b) result(c) Return the lower-valued operand with its derivative, choosing a on a tie. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_min_real(a, b) result(c) Select the minimum of AD a and constant b; selecting b clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_min_ad(a, b) result(c) Select the minimum of constant a and AD b; selecting a clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\min.html"},{"title":"operator(*) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(*) Multiplication using the product rule. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_multiply(a, b) result(c) Apply the product rule: d(a b) = da b + a*db. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_multiply_real(a, b) result(c) Scale the value and derivative by a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_multiply_ad(a, b) result(c) Multiply a real64 constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_multiply_integer(a, b) result(c) Scale an AD operand by a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_multiply_ad(a, b) result(c) Multiply a default-integer constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(ASTERISK).html"},{"title":"operator(**) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(**) Exponentiation with constant or variable base/exponent.\nVariable exponents require a positive base, except that a zero constant\nbase with a positive exponent has zero derivative. Constant integral\nexponents also support negative bases. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_power(a, b) result(c) Apply d(a b) = b*a (b-1) da + a b log(a)*db.\nOmit inactive terms so constant powers work at zero and negative bases. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_power_real(a, b) result(c) Raise AD a to constant b with derivative b a (b-1) da.\nExponents zero and one are handled without singular intermediate powers. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_power_ad(a, b) result(c) Raise constant a to AD b with derivative a b log(a) db.\nA zero base and positive exponent give zero for both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_power_integer(a, b) result(c) Evaluate an integer power, preserving negative-base and zero-base behavior.\nNegative exponents avoid b-1, which could overflow the integer range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_power_ad(a, b) result(c) Raise a default-integer constant to an AD exponent using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(ASTERISKASTERISK).html"},{"title":"operator(+) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(+) Unary identity and addition, including constant operands in either order. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_add(a, b) result(c) Add values and directional derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_add_real(a, b) result(c) Add a real64 constant without changing the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_add_ad(a, b) result(c) Add an AD operand to a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_add_integer(a, b) result(c) Add a default-integer constant using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_add_ad(a, b) result(c) Add an AD operand to a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_positive(a) result(c) Unary plus preserves both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(+).html"},{"title":"operator(-) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(-) Unary negation and subtraction, including constant operands. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_subtract(a, b) result(c) Subtract values and directional derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_subtract_real(a, b) result(c) Subtract a real64 constant without changing the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_subtract_ad(a, b) result(c) Subtract an AD operand from a real64 constant, negating its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_subtract_integer(a, b) result(c) Subtract a default-integer constant using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_subtract_ad(a, b) result(c) Subtract an AD operand from a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_negative(a) result(c) Unary minus negates both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(-).html"},{"title":"operator(/) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(/) Division using the quotient rule; the denominator must be nonzero. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_divide(a, b) result(c) Apply the quotient rule as d(a/b) = (da - (a/b)*db)/b. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_divide_real(a, b) result(c) Divide the value and derivative by a nonzero real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_divide_ad(a, b) result(c) Divide a real64 constant by AD b, with derivative -a db/b *2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_divide_integer(a, b) result(c) Divide an AD operand by a nonzero default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_divide_ad(a, b) result(c) Divide a default-integer constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(SLASH).html"},{"title":"operator(/=) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(/=) Inequality of values, independent of derivative seeds. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_not_equal(a, b) result(c) Compare only the values of two AD operands for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_not_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a real64 constant for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_not_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a real64 constant with an AD value for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_not_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a default integer for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_not_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a default integer with an AD value for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(SLASH=).html"},{"title":"operator(<) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(<) Strict less-than comparison of values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_less(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is strictly less than AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is less than a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_less_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is less than an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is less than a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_less_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is less than an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(lt).html"},{"title":"operator(<=) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(<=) Less-than-or-equal comparison of values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_less_equal(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is less than or equal to AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at most a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_less_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is at most an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at most a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_less_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is at most an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(lt=).html"},{"title":"operator(==) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(==) Equality of values, independent of derivative seeds. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_equal(a, b) result(c) Compare only the values of two AD operands for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a real64 constant for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a real64 constant with an AD value for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a default integer for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a default integer with an AD value for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(==).html"},{"title":"operator(>) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(>) Strict greater-than comparison of values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_greater(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is strictly greater than AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value exceeds a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_greater_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant exceeds an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value exceeds a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_greater_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer exceeds an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(gt).html"},{"title":"operator(>=) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface operator(>=) Greater-than-or-equal comparison of values. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_greater_equal(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is greater than or equal to AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at least a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_greater_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is at least an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at least a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_greater_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is at least an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface\\operator(gt=).html"},{"title":"sign – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface sign Magnitude of a with the sign of b; ignores the derivative of b. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_sign(a, b) result(c) Propagate sign(1,b)*d(abs(a)), treating the sign selection as constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_sign_real(a, b) result(c) Apply a constant sign to AD a and its absolute-value derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_sign_ad(a, b) result(c) Apply AD b's sign to a constant magnitude, returning derivative zero. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\sign.html"},{"title":"sin – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface sin Sine, with arguments in radians. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_sin(a) result(c) Propagate cos(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\sin.html"},{"title":"sinh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface sinh Hyperbolic sine. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_sinh(a) result(c) Propagate cosh(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\sinh.html"},{"title":"sqrt – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface sqrt Square root for nonnegative values; its active derivative is singular at zero. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_sqrt(a) result(c) Propagate da/(2*sqrt(a)); inactive seeds remain zero at a = 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\sqrt.html"},{"title":"tan – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface tan Tangent, with arguments in radians and away from its poles. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_tan(a) result(c) Propagate da/cos(a)**2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\tan.html"},{"title":"tanh – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface tanh Hyperbolic tangent. Module Procedures private elemental function ad_tanh(a) result(c) Propagate da/cosh(a)**2 using exp(-abs(a)) to avoid hyperbolic overflow. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad )","tags":"","url":"interface\\tanh.html"},{"title":"write_ode_results – DIFFEQ","text":"public  subroutine write_ode_results(fname, rst, delimiter) Writes the contents of a ode_results container to a delimited text\nfile, replacing any existing file.  Each row contains the independent\nvariable followed by the state variables, without a header.  An\ninitialized empty container produces an empty file.  Invalid delimiters\ncause DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR; uninitialized containers and file I/O\nfailures cause DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: fname The name of the file to write. class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: rst The ode_results container to write. character(len=1), intent(in), optional :: delimiter The field delimiter.  The default is a comma.  The delimiter\nmust not be a double quote, carriage return, or line feed.","tags":"","url":"proc\\write_ode_results.html"},{"title":"c_get_ode_results – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_get_ode_results(c_obj, m, n, x, ldx) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results\") Returns the contents of the ode_results object as a matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: m The number of rows in x. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: n The number of columns in x. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: x (ldx,n) The matrix where the results are written.  The matrix is stored\nin column-major format with the first column containing the\nindependent variable values at which the integrator returned\na solution point.  The remaining columns each contain a state\nvariable. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: ldx The leading dimension of matrix x.  This value must be at least\nm. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_get_ode_results.html"},{"title":"c_get_ode_results_size – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_get_ode_results_size(c_obj, rows, cols) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results_size\") Gets the size of the matrix required to hold the integration results. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: rows The number of rows in the matrix. integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: cols The number of columns in the matrix. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_get_ode_results_size.html"},{"title":"c_get_ode_results_statistics – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_get_ode_results_statistics(c_obj, stats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results_statistics\") Gets the integrator performance statistics from an ode_results object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: stats A c_ode_results_statistics container for the results. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_get_ode_results_statistics.html"},{"title":"c_write_ode_results – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_write_ode_results(fname, c_obj, delimiter) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_write_ode_results\") Writes the contents of an ode_results container to a\ndelimited text file. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in) :: fname (*) The filename. type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in), value :: delimiter The delimiter character. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_write_ode_results.html"},{"title":"c_create_ode_results – DIFFEQ","text":"public  subroutine c_create_ode_results(c_obj, src) Constructs a new ode_results pointer and returns its address to\nthe supplied C pointer.  Be sure to call c_free_ode_results once\nfinished with this object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: c_obj A pointer to the newly created ode_results object. type( ode_results ), intent(in) :: src The source ode_results object.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_create_ode_results.html"},{"title":"c_default_ode_event_solver_settings – DIFFEQ","text":"public  subroutine c_default_ode_event_solver_settings(settings) bind(C, name = \"c_default_ode_event_solver_settings\") Populates a c_ode_event_solver_settings object with default\nvalues. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_event_solver_settings ), intent(out) :: settings The c_ode_event_solver_settings object.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_default_ode_event_solver_settings.html"},{"title":"c_free_ode_results – DIFFEQ","text":"public  subroutine c_free_ode_results(c_obj) bind(C, name = \"c_free_ode_results\") Frees memory allocated by c_create_ode_results. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj A pointer to the ode_results object to free.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_free_ode_results.html"},{"title":"assignment(=) – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface assignment(=) Module Procedures private  subroutine c_ode_results_stats_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( ode_results_statistics ) :: rhs private  subroutine ode_results_stats_to_c_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs private  subroutine c_ode_event_stats_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( ode_event_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs private  subroutine ode_event_stats_to_c_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs","tags":"","url":"interface\\assignment(=)~2.html"},{"title":"evaluate_newton_polynomial – DIFFEQ","text":"public pure subroutine evaluate_newton_polynomial(x, d, xi, y) Evaluates a polynomial stored in Newton divided-difference form. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An M-element array containing the interpolation nodes. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: d An N-by-M matrix containing the divided-difference coefficients. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: xi The value at which to evaluate the polynomial. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y An N-element array where the result will be written.","tags":"","url":"proc\\evaluate_newton_polynomial.html"},{"title":"newton_divided_differences – DIFFEQ","text":"public pure subroutine newton_divided_differences(x, y, d) Computes the Newton divided-difference coefficients of the polynomial\ninterpolating the supplied points. The resulting coefficients define Divided differences are symmetric in their arguments, so the nodes need\nnot be sorted.  Storing them most-recent-first keeps the terms of the\nextrapolation in decreasing order of significance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x An M-element array containing the interpolation nodes. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: y An N-by-M matrix whose columns contain the values at each node. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: d An N-by-M matrix where the coefficients will be written.","tags":"","url":"proc\\newton_divided_differences.html"},{"title":"build_linearized_system – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine build_linearized_system(this, sys, h, x, y, A, b, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( newton_multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The newton_multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current value(s) of the dependent variable(s). real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: A The N-by-N matrix , where, for BDF methods at least, . real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: b The N-element right-hand-side vector for the linear system.\nThis vector is the negative of the corrector residual so\nthat the Newton update is . class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. Description Builds the linearized system used to compute the solution for the\nimplicit step via Newton iteration.  This routine forms matrices and of the system .","tags":"","url":"interface\\build_linearized_system.html"},{"title":"multistep_corrector – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine multistep_corrector(this, sys, h, x, ypred, ynew, converged, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: ypred The N-element array containing the predicted values at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: ynew The new estimate of the dependent variables. logical, intent(out) :: converged True if the corrector succeeded; else, false, in which case\nthe step is retried on a shorter step size. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. Description Refines the prediction by applying the implicit formula.","tags":"","url":"interface\\multistep_corrector.html"},{"title":"multistep_error_constant – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public pure function multistep_error_constant(this, k) result(rst) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: k The order of interest. Return Value real(kind=real64) The error constant. Description Returns the constant relating the difference between the\ncorrected and predicted solutions to the local truncation error\nof the method at the requested order.","tags":"","url":"interface\\multistep_error_constant.html"},{"title":"multistep_integer_inquiry – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public pure function multistep_integer_inquiry(this) result(rst) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. Return Value integer The requested value. Description Returns an integer value from the multistep_integrator object.","tags":"","url":"interface\\multistep_integer_inquiry.html"},{"title":"predictor_step – DIFFEQ","text":"interface public  subroutine predictor_step(this, sys, h, x, y, f, yn, fn, args) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current value(s) of the dependent variable(s). real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives\nat x.  For a system carrying a mass matrix these are the\nvalues of rather than of . real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nsolution estimate at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nderivative estimate at x + h. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. Description Evaluates the predictor. Besides supplying the initial estimate for the Newton iteration,\nthis routine is the natural place for a concrete integrator to\ncompute any step-dependent quantities, such as method\ncoefficients, that the corrector requires.  It is called exactly\nonce per step attempt.","tags":"","url":"interface\\predictor_step.html"},{"title":"ggl_container – DIFFEQ","text":"public interface ggl_container Module Procedures private  function ggl_constructor_1(coordinate_count, constraint_count, alpha, beta) result(rst) Defines the mechanical dimensions and resets stabilization gains to one\nunless supplied. Callback associations and inherited model options are\nretained. Invalid counts or gains cause DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: coordinate_count Positive number N of coordinates and physical velocities. integer, intent(in) :: constraint_count Number M of independent constraints, with 1 <= M <= N. real(kind=real64), intent(in), optional :: alpha Nonnegative finite position and velocity decay rates, respectively,\nin inverse independent-variable units. Zero disables the respective\ndamping term without disabling the differentiated constraint. real(kind=real64), intent(in), optional :: beta Nonnegative finite position and velocity decay rates, respectively,\nin inverse independent-variable units. Zero disables the respective\ndamping term without disabling the differentiated constraint. Return Value type( ggl_container ) The new ggl_container object.","tags":"","url":"interface\\ggl_container.html"},{"title":"c_adams – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_adams(nx, nstates, fcn, x, initcond, settings, mass, output) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_adams\") Utilizes a variable order Adams predictor-corrector integrator to \nsolve a system of first order differential equations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations.  This value must be at least 1;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: fcn A pointer to the function containing the equations to integrate. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: mass A pointer to the routine for computing the mass matrix.  Pass\nNULL if no routine is necessary.  This routine cannot handle\nsingular mass matrices. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_adams.html"},{"title":"c_adams_events – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_adams_events(nx, nstates, nevents, fcn, x, initcond, settings, esettings, efcn, mass, output, estats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_adams_events\") Utilizes a variable order Adams predictor-corrector integrator to \nsolve a system of first order differential equations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations.  This value must be at least 1;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nevents The number of event equations. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: fcn A pointer to the function containing the equations to integrate. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type( c_ode_event_solver_settings ), intent(in) :: esettings The event solver settings. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: efcn A pointer to the function containing the event equations. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: mass A pointer to the routine for computing the mass matrix.  Pass\nNULL if no routine is necessary.  This routine cannot handle\nsingular mass matrices. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: estats Event detection solver results and statistics. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_adams_events.html"},{"title":"c_bdf – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_bdf(nx, nstates, fcn, x, initcond, settings, jac, mass, output) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_bdf\") Utilizes a variable order BDF integrator to solve a system of \nfirst order differential equations or index-1 differential \nalgebraic equations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations.  This value must be at least 1;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: fcn A pointer to the function containing the equations to integrate. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: jac A pointer to the routine for computing the Jacobian matrix.\nPass NULL if no routine is necessary and allowing the integrator\nto use a finite-difference estimate is acceptable. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: mass A pointer to the routine for computing the mass matrix.  Pass\nNULL if no routine is necessary. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_bdf.html"},{"title":"c_bdf_events – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_bdf_events(nx, nstates, nevents, fcn, x, initcond, settings, esettings, efcn, jac, mass, output, estats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_bdf_events\") Utilizes a variable order BDF integrator to solve a system of \nfirst order differential equations or index-1 differential \nalgebraic equations. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations.  This value must be at least 1;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nevents The number of event equations. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: fcn A pointer to the function containing the equations to integrate. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type( c_ode_event_solver_settings ), intent(in) :: esettings The event solver settings. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: efcn A pointer to the function containing the event equations. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: jac A pointer to the routine for computing the Jacobian matrix.\nPass NULL if no routine is necessary and allowing the integrator\nto use a finite-difference estimate is acceptable. type(c_funptr), intent(in), value :: mass A pointer to the routine for computing the mass matrix.  Pass\nNULL if no routine is necessary. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: estats Event detection solver results and statistics. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_bdf_events.html"},{"title":"c_dae_bdf – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_dae_bdf(model, nx, nstates, x, initcond, settings, output, estats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_dae_bdf\") Utilizes a variable order BDF integrator to solve the system of\nDAE's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ggl_container ), intent(in) :: model The c_ggl_container containing the constraints and model. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations, including the constraints.  This \nvalue must be at least 1; else, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is \nreturned. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(inout) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: estats Event detection solver results and statistics. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_dae_bdf.html"},{"title":"c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_4 – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_4(model, nx, nstates, x, initcond, settings, output, estats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_4\") Utilizes a 4th order Kennedy-Carpenter integrator to solve the \nsystem of DAE's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ggl_container ), intent(in) :: model The c_ggl_container containing the constraints and model. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nx The number of solution points.  This value must be at least 2;\nelse, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is returned. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: nstates The number of state equations, including the constraints.  This \nvalue must be at least 1; else, a C_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR is \nreturned. real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: x (nx) An NX-element array containing the desired solution points. real(kind=c_double), intent(inout) :: initcond (nstates) An NSTATES-element array containing the initial conditions. type( c_ode_settings ), intent(in) :: settings The integrator settings. type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: output The output c_ode_results object.  Memory must be freed by \nc_free_ode_results. type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: estats Event detection solver results and statistics. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation.","tags":"","url":"proc\\c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_4.html"},{"title":"c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_5 – DIFFEQ","text":"public  function c_dae_kennedy_carpenter_5(model, nx, nstates,