p size PI control parameter. procedure, public :: set_step_size_factor => oi_set_safety_factor Sets the step size safety factor. procedure, public :: solve => ssi_ode_solver Solves the supplied system of ODE's.","tags":"","url":"module\\diffeq_rk45.html"},{"title":"diffeq_auto_diff – DIFFEQ","text":"First-order forward automatic differentiation for Jacobian expressions. Each real_ad stores one value and one directional derivative. Reevaluate\nan expression with one independent variable seeded at a time to obtain\nJacobian columns. All overloads are elemental and preserve scalar expansion.\nArithmetic and comparisons accept real_ad, real(real64), and default\ninteger operands; binary intrinsics accept real_ad and real(real64). Comparisons ignore derivatives. ABS uses derivative zero at zero; MIN/MAX\nare binary and retain the first argument on ties. SIGN differentiates only\nits magnitude argument. These are branch conventions, not derivatives at\ndiscontinuities. Other domain errors and singular derivatives follow the\nunderlying real intrinsics and the caller's floating-point error settings. In the procedures below, a/b (or y/x for ATAN2) are input operands, c is\nthe result, and dx is propagated by the chain rule. Real and integer\noperands are constants with derivative zero. Uses iso_fortran_env Interfaces public        interface abs Absolute value; the derivative at zero is defined to be zero. private elemental function ad_abs(a) result(c) Propagate sign(a)*da, choosing derivative zero at a = 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface acos Inverse cosine in radians; the active derivative is singular at +/-1. private elemental function ad_acos(a) result(c) Propagate -da/sqrt(1-a**2) using the inverse-sine derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface acosh Inverse hyperbolic cosine for values >= 1; active derivative singular at 1. private elemental function ad_acosh(a) result(c) Propagate da/(sqrt(a-1)*sqrt(a+1)); inactive seeds stay zero at a = 1. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface asin Inverse sine in radians; the active derivative is singular at +/-1. private elemental function ad_asin(a) result(c) Propagate da/sqrt(1-a**2), omitting the singular term for inactive seeds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface asinh Inverse hyperbolic sine. private elemental function ad_asinh(a) result(c) Propagate da/sqrt(a**2+1), using HYPOT to avoid overflow. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface assignment(=) Copy AD data, assign a constant (clearing dx), or extract a real value. private elemental subroutine ad_assign_1(lhs, rhs) Copy the value and derivative of rhs to lhs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_2(lhs, rhs) Assign a real64 constant rhs to lhs and clear its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_3(lhs, rhs) Extract the value of rhs into real64 lhs, discarding the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: lhs type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: rhs private elemental subroutine ad_assign_integer(lhs, rhs) Assign a default-integer constant rhs to lhs and clear its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(out) :: lhs integer, intent(in) :: rhs public        interface atan One- or two-argument inverse tangent in radians. private elemental function ad_atan(a) result(c) Propagate da/(1+a**2), using HYPOT to avoid squaring large a. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2(y, x) result(c) Propagate (x dy-y dx)/(x 2+y 2) using a scaled radius. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2_real(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with AD ordinate y and constant abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_atan2_ad(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with constant ordinate y and AD abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface atan2 Quadrant-aware inverse tangent ATAN2(y,x); not defined at the origin. private elemental function ad_atan2(y, x) result(c) Propagate (x dy-y dx)/(x 2+y 2) using a scaled radius. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_atan2_real(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with AD ordinate y and constant abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: y real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_atan2_ad(y, x) result(c) Evaluate ATAN2 with constant ordinate y and AD abscissa x. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: x Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface atanh Inverse hyperbolic tangent for values strictly between -1 and 1. private elemental function ad_atanh(a) result(c) Propagate da/(1-a**2) using factored divisions. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface cos Cosine, with arguments in radians. private elemental function ad_cos(a) result(c) Propagate -sin(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface cosh Hyperbolic cosine. private elemental function ad_cosh(a) result(c) Propagate sinh(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface erf Error function. private elemental function ad_erf(a) result(c) Propagate 2/sqrt(pi) exp(-a 2) da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface erfc Complementary error function. private elemental function ad_erfc(a) result(c) Negate the error-function derivative for the complementary error function. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface exp Natural exponential. private elemental function ad_exp(a) result(c) Propagate exp(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface log Natural logarithm for positive values. private elemental function ad_log(a) result(c) Propagate da/a for the natural logarithm. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface log10 Base-ten logarithm for positive values. private elemental function ad_log10(a) result(c) Propagate da/(a*log(10)) for the base-ten logarithm. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface max Binary maximum, carrying the selected derivative; first argument wins ties. private elemental function ad_max(a, b) result(c) Return the higher-valued operand with its derivative, choosing a on a tie. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_max_real(a, b) result(c) Select the maximum of AD a and constant b; selecting b clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_max_ad(a, b) result(c) Select the maximum of constant a and AD b; selecting a clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface min Binary minimum, carrying the selected derivative; first argument wins ties. private elemental function ad_min(a, b) result(c) Return the lower-valued operand with its derivative, choosing a on a tie. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_min_real(a, b) result(c) Select the minimum of AD a and constant b; selecting b clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_min_ad(a, b) result(c) Select the minimum of constant a and AD b; selecting a clears the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(*) Multiplication using the product rule. private elemental function ad_multiply(a, b) result(c) Apply the product rule: d(a b) = da b + a*db. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_multiply_real(a, b) result(c) Scale the value and derivative by a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_multiply_ad(a, b) result(c) Multiply a real64 constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_multiply_integer(a, b) result(c) Scale an AD operand by a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_multiply_ad(a, b) result(c) Multiply a default-integer constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(**) Exponentiation with constant or variable base/exponent.\nVariable exponents require a positive base, except that a zero constant\nbase with a positive exponent has zero derivative. Constant integral\nexponents also support negative bases. private elemental function ad_power(a, b) result(c) Apply d(a b) = b*a (b-1) da + a b log(a)*db.\nOmit inactive terms so constant powers work at zero and negative bases. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_power_real(a, b) result(c) Raise AD a to constant b with derivative b a (b-1) da.\nExponents zero and one are handled without singular intermediate powers. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_power_ad(a, b) result(c) Raise constant a to AD b with derivative a b log(a) db.\nA zero base and positive exponent give zero for both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_power_integer(a, b) result(c) Evaluate an integer power, preserving negative-base and zero-base behavior.\nNegative exponents avoid b-1, which could overflow the integer range. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_power_ad(a, b) result(c) Raise a default-integer constant to an AD exponent using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(+) Unary identity and addition, including constant operands in either order. private elemental function ad_add(a, b) result(c) Add values and directional derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_add_real(a, b) result(c) Add a real64 constant without changing the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_add_ad(a, b) result(c) Add an AD operand to a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_add_integer(a, b) result(c) Add a default-integer constant using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_add_ad(a, b) result(c) Add an AD operand to a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_positive(a) result(c) Unary plus preserves both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(-) Unary negation and subtraction, including constant operands. private elemental function ad_subtract(a, b) result(c) Subtract values and directional derivatives. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_subtract_real(a, b) result(c) Subtract a real64 constant without changing the derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_subtract_ad(a, b) result(c) Subtract an AD operand from a real64 constant, negating its derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_subtract_integer(a, b) result(c) Subtract a default-integer constant using real64 arithmetic. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_subtract_ad(a, b) result(c) Subtract an AD operand from a default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_negative(a) result(c) Unary minus negates both components. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(/) Division using the quotient rule; the denominator must be nonzero. private elemental function ad_divide(a, b) result(c) Apply the quotient rule as d(a/b) = (da - (a/b)*db)/b. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_divide_real(a, b) result(c) Divide the value and derivative by a nonzero real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_divide_ad(a, b) result(c) Divide a real64 constant by AD b, with derivative -a db/b *2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_divide_integer(a, b) result(c) Divide an AD operand by a nonzero default-integer constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function integer_divide_ad(a, b) result(c) Divide a default-integer constant by an AD operand. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface operator(/=) Inequality of values, independent of derivative seeds. private elemental function ad_not_equal(a, b) result(c) Compare only the values of two AD operands for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_not_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a real64 constant for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_not_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a real64 constant with an AD value for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_not_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a default integer for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_not_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a default integer with an AD value for inequality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface operator(<) Strict less-than comparison of values. private elemental function ad_less(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is strictly less than AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is less than a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_less_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is less than an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is less than a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_less_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is less than an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface operator(<=) Less-than-or-equal comparison of values. private elemental function ad_less_equal(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is less than or equal to AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at most a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_less_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is at most an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_less_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at most a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_less_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is at most an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface operator(==) Equality of values, independent of derivative seeds. private elemental function ad_equal(a, b) result(c) Compare only the values of two AD operands for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a real64 constant for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a real64 constant with an AD value for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Compare an AD value with a default integer for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Compare a default integer with an AD value for equality. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface operator(>) Strict greater-than comparison of values. private elemental function ad_greater(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is strictly greater than AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value exceeds a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_greater_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant exceeds an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value exceeds a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_greater_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer exceeds an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface operator(>=) Greater-than-or-equal comparison of values. private elemental function ad_greater_equal(a, b) result(c) Test whether AD a's value is greater than or equal to AD b's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_equal_real(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at least a real64 constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function real_greater_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a real64 constant is at least an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function ad_greater_equal_integer(a, b) result(c) Test whether an AD value is at least a default integer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: b Return Value logical private elemental function integer_greater_equal_ad(a, b) result(c) Test whether a default integer is at least an AD value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value logical public        interface sign Magnitude of a with the sign of b; ignores the derivative of b. private elemental function ad_sign(a, b) result(c) Propagate sign(1,b)*d(abs(a)), treating the sign selection as constant. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function ad_sign_real(a, b) result(c) Apply a constant sign to AD a and its absolute-value derivative. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) private elemental function real_sign_ad(a, b) result(c) Apply AD b's sign to a constant magnitude, returning derivative zero. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: a type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: b Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface sin Sine, with arguments in radians. private elemental function ad_sin(a) result(c) Propagate cos(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface sinh Hyperbolic sine. private elemental function ad_sinh(a) result(c) Propagate cosh(a)*da. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface sqrt Square root for nonnegative values; its active derivative is singular at zero. private elemental function ad_sqrt(a) result(c) Propagate da/(2*sqrt(a)); inactive seeds remain zero at a = 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface tan Tangent, with arguments in radians and away from its poles. private elemental function ad_tan(a) result(c) Propagate da/cos(a)**2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) public        interface tanh Hyperbolic tangent. private elemental function ad_tanh(a) result(c) Propagate da/cosh(a)**2 using exp(-abs(a)) to avoid hyperbolic overflow. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( real_ad ), intent(in) :: a Return Value type( real_ad ) Derived Types type, public :: real_ad A value and its directional derivative. Seed dx with one for an\nindependent variable and zero for constants. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=real64), public :: dx Directional derivative with respect to the current seed. real(kind=real64), public :: x Function or independent-variable value.","tags":"","url":"module\\diffeq_auto_diff.html"},{"title":"diffeq_container_io – DIFFEQ","text":"Uses diffeq_errors iso_fortran_env diffeq_containers Subroutines public  subroutine write_ode_results (fname, rst, delimiter) Writes the contents of a ode_results container to a delimited text\nfile, replacing any existing file.  Each row contains the independent\nvariable followed by the state variables, without a header.  An\ninitialized empty container produces an empty file.  Invalid delimiters\ncause DIFFEQ_INVALID_INPUT_ERROR; uninitialized containers and file I/O\nfailures cause DIFFEQ_INVALID_OPERATION_ERROR. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: fname The name of the file to write. class( ode_results ), intent(in) :: rst The ode_results container to write. character(len=1), intent(in), optional :: delimiter The field delimiter.  The default is a comma.  The delimiter\nmust not be a double quote, carriage return, or line feed.","tags":"","url":"module\\diffeq_container_io.html"},{"title":"diffeq_c_containers – DIFFEQ","text":"Uses diffeq_base diffeq_container_io diffeq_containers diffeq_c_helpers iso_c_binding diffeq_c_errors Interfaces public        interface assignment(=) private  subroutine c_ode_results_stats_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( ode_results_statistics ) :: rhs private  subroutine ode_results_stats_to_c_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs private  subroutine c_ode_event_stats_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( ode_event_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs private  subroutine ode_event_stats_to_c_assign(lhs, rhs) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ode_event_statistics ), intent(out) :: lhs type( c_ode_event_statistics ), intent(in) :: rhs Derived Types type, public, bind(C) :: c_ode_event_solver_settings A container for ODE event solver settings. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=c_int), public :: max_allowed_iterations = 1000 The maximum number of allowed iterations. real(kind=c_double), public :: tolerance = 1.0d-12 The iteration convergence tolerance. type, public, bind(C) :: c_ode_event_statistics An ODE event solver statistics container. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=c_int), public :: event_index = -1 The zero-based index of the event equation where an event was \nlocated.  If no event was found, this value is set to -1. integer(kind=c_int), public :: function_evaluations = 0 The number of event function evaluations. integer(kind=c_int), public :: iteration_count = 0 The number of iterations taken by the solver. type, public, bind(C) :: c_ode_results_statistics A container of performance statistics for an\nintegrator. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=c_int), public :: failed_steps = 0 The number of unsuccessful steps taken by the integrator. integer(kind=c_int), public :: function_evaluations = 0 The number of function evaluations. integer(kind=c_int), public :: jacobian_evaluations = 0 The number of Jacobian matrix evaluations. integer(kind=c_int), public :: matrix_factorizations = 0 The number of matrix factorizations. integer(kind=c_int), public :: successful_steps = 0 The number of successful steps taken by the integrator. Functions public  function c_get_ode_results (c_obj, m, n, x, ldx) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results\") Returns the contents of the ode_results object as a matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: m The number of rows in x. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: n The number of columns in x. real(kind=c_double), intent(out) :: x (ldx,n) The matrix where the results are written.  The matrix is stored\nin column-major format with the first column containing the\nindependent variable values at which the integrator returned\na solution point.  The remaining columns each contain a state\nvariable. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), value :: ldx The leading dimension of matrix x.  This value must be at least\nm. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation. public  function c_get_ode_results_size (c_obj, rows, cols) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results_size\") Gets the size of the matrix required to hold the integration results. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: rows The number of rows in the matrix. integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: cols The number of columns in the matrix. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation. public  function c_get_ode_results_statistics (c_obj, stats) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_get_ode_results_statistics\") Gets the integrator performance statistics from an ode_results object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. type( c_ode_results_statistics ), intent(out) :: stats A c_ode_results_statistics container for the results. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation. public  function c_write_ode_results (fname, c_obj, delimiter) result(rst) bind(C, name = \"c_write_ode_results\") Writes the contents of an ode_results container to a\ndelimited text file. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in) :: fname (*) The filename. type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj The pointer to the ode_results object. character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in), value :: delimiter The delimiter character. Return Value integer(kind=c_int) An error flag denoting the status of the operation. Subroutines public  subroutine c_create_ode_results (c_obj, src) Constructs a new ode_results pointer and returns its address to\nthe supplied C pointer.  Be sure to call c_free_ode_results once\nfinished with this object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(out) :: c_obj A pointer to the newly created ode_results object. type( ode_results ), intent(in) :: src The source ode_results object. public  subroutine c_default_ode_event_solver_settings (settings) bind(C, name = \"c_default_ode_event_solver_settings\") Populates a c_ode_event_solver_settings object with default\nvalues. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( c_ode_event_solver_settings ), intent(out) :: settings The c_ode_event_solver_settings object. public  subroutine c_free_ode_results (c_obj) bind(C, name = \"c_free_ode_results\") Frees memory allocated by c_create_ode_results. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(in), value :: c_obj A pointer to the ode_results object to free.","tags":"","url":"module\\diffeq_c_containers.html"},{"title":"diffeq_rk853_constants – DIFFEQ","text":"Uses iso_fortran_env Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a101 = 4.77662536438264365890433908527d-1 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a104 = -2.48811461997166764192642586468d0 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a105 = -5.90290826836842996371446475743d-1 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a106 = 2.12300514481811942347288949897d1 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a107 = 1.52792336328824235832596922938d1 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a108 = -3.32882109689848629194453265587d1 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a109 = -2.03312017085086261358222928593d-2 real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: a111 = -9.3714243008598732571704021658d-1 real(kind=real64), public, param