ts Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ode_event_solver ), public :: event_solver The ODE event solver.  Enable event detection by defining the\nevent_function in the ode_container object. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: append_to_buffer => oi_append_to_buffer Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution \nbuffer. procedure, public :: attempt_step => tsit_attempt_step Attempts an integration step for this integrator. procedure, public :: clear_buffer => oi_clear_buffer Clears the contents of the buffer. procedure, public :: compute_dense_output => ssi_dense_output procedure, public :: compute_error_norm => oi_estimate_error Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate. procedure, public :: estimate_inital_step_size => oi_initial_step Computes an estimate of an initial step size. procedure, public :: estimate_next_step_size => oi_next_step Estimates the next step size. procedure, public :: evaluate_dense => oi_evaluate_dense Evaluates the prepared step without advancing integration. procedure, public :: get_absolute_tolerance => oi_get_abs_tol Gets the absolute error tolerance. procedure, public :: get_allow_overshoot => oi_get_allow_overshoot Gets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. procedure, public :: get_dense_interval => oi_get_dense_interval Gets the prepared step's start and end in integration order. procedure, public :: get_dense_output_enabled => oi_get_dense_enabled Gets the explicit dense-output preparation setting. procedure, public :: get_is_fsal => tsit_get_is_fsal Gets a logical parameter stating if this is a first-same-as-last\n(FSAL) integrator. procedure, public :: get_maximum_step_size => oi_get_max_step Gets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. procedure, public :: get_minimum_step_size => oi_get_min_step Gets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. procedure, public :: get_ode_results => oi_get_ode_results Returns the solution stored within an ode_results object. procedure, public :: get_order => tsit_get_order Gets the order of the integrator. procedure, public :: get_relative_tolerance => oi_get_rel_tol Gets the relative error tolerance. procedure, public :: get_solution => oi_get_solution Returns the solution computed by the integrator. procedure, public :: get_stage_count => tsit_get_stage_count Gets the stage count for this integrator. procedure, public :: get_step_limit => oi_get_step_limit Gets the limit on the number of integration steps. procedure, public :: get_step_size_control_parameter => oi_get_control_parameter Gets the step size PI control parameter. procedure, public :: get_step_size_factor => oi_get_safety_factor Gets the step size safety factor. procedure, public :: has_dense_output => oi_has_dense_output Tests whether a prepared accepted-step interpolant is available. procedure, public :: interpolate => tsit_interpolate Performs the interpolation. procedure, public :: invalidate_dense_output => oi_invalidate_dense Invalidates the prepared interpolant before stepping or resetting. procedure, public :: log_failed_step => oi_log_failed_step Logs a failed integration step. procedure, public :: log_function_evaluation => oi_log_function_eval Logs a function evaluation. procedure, public :: log_jacobian_evaluation => oi_log_jacobian_eval Logs a Jacobian matrix evaluation. procedure, public :: log_matrix_factorization => oi_log_matrix_factorization Logs a matrix factorization. procedure, public :: log_successful_step => oi_log_successful_step Logs a successful integration step. procedure, public :: post_step_action => tsit_post_step Performs any post-step actions. procedure, public :: pre_step_action => tsit_pre_step Performs any pre-step actions. generic, public :: set_absolute_tolerance => oi_set_abs_tol, oi_set_abs_tols Sets the absolute error tolerance. procedure, public :: set_allow_overshoot => oi_set_allow_overshoot Sets a value determining if the solver is allowed to overshoot \nthe final value in the integration range. procedure, public :: set_dense_interval => oi_set_dense_interval Implementation hook publishing a prepared accepted step. procedure, public :: set_dense_output_enabled => oi_set_dense_enabled Enables dense output on every accepted step (default: false). procedure, public :: set_maximum_step_size => oi_set_max_step Sets the magnitude of the maximum allowed step size. procedure, public :: set_minimum_step_size => oi_set_min_step Sets the magnitude of the minimum allowed step size. generic, public :: set_relative_tolerance => oi_set_rel_tol, oi_set_rel_tols Sets the relative error tolerance. procedure, public :: set_step_limit => oi_set_step_limit Sets the limit on the number of integration steps. procedure, public :: set_step_size_control_parameter => oi_set_control_parameter Sets the step size PI control parameter. procedure, public :: set_step_size_factor => oi_set_safety_factor Sets the step size safety factor. procedure, public :: solve => ssi_ode_solver Solves the supplied system of ODE's.","tags":"","url":"module\\diffeq_tsitouras.html"},{"title":"diffeq_multistep – DIFFEQ","text":"Provides the base structure for implicit, variable step-size, variable\norder, multi-step integrators. A multi-step method advances a system written as by relating the solution at to several previously accepted\nsolution points rather than to intermediate stage values.  The routines\ncollected here supply the machinery common to such methods: storage and\nmanagement of the solution history, Newton iteration on the implicit\ncorrector equation, polynomial interpolation of the history for both\nprediction and dense output, and the adaptive step-size and order\ncontroller. A concrete integrator supplies only the method-specific pieces by\nimplementing predictor, correct, get_maximum_supported_order,\nget_error_constant, and get_truncation_constant.  Methods whose\ncorrector equation is solved by Newton iteration should extend\nnewton_multistep_integrator, which supplies that corrector. Uses diffeq_base linalg diffeq_errors iso_fortran_env Interfaces interface public  subroutine build_linearized_system(this, sys, h, x, y, A, b, args) Builds the linearized system used to compute the solution for the\nimplicit step via Newton iteration.  This routine forms matrices and of the system . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( newton_multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The newton_multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current value(s) of the dependent variable(s). real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: A The N-by-N matrix , where, for BDF methods at least, . real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: b The N-element right-hand-side vector for the linear system.\nThis vector is the negative of the corrector residual so\nthat the Newton update is . class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. interface public  subroutine multistep_corrector(this, sys, h, x, ypred, ynew, converged, args) Refines the prediction by applying the implicit formula. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: ypred The N-element array containing the predicted values at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: ynew The new estimate of the dependent variables. logical, intent(out) :: converged True if the corrector succeeded; else, false, in which case\nthe step is retried on a shorter step size. class(*), intent(inout), optional, target :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. interface public pure function multistep_error_constant(this, k) result(rst) Returns the constant relating the difference between the\ncorrected and predicted solutions to the local truncation error\nof the method at the requested order. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. integer, intent(in) :: k The order of interest. Return Value real(kind=real64) The error constant. interface public pure function multistep_integer_inquiry(this) result(rst) Returns an integer value from the multistep_integrator object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(in) :: this The multistep_integrator object. Return Value integer The requested value. interface public  subroutine predictor_step(this, sys, h, x, y, f, yn, fn, args) Evaluates the predictor. Besides supplying the initial estimate for the Newton iteration,\nthis routine is the natural place for a concrete integrator to\ncompute any step-dependent quantities, such as method\ncoefficients, that the corrector requires.  It is called exactly\nonce per step attempt. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multistep_integrator ), intent(inout) :: this The multistep_integrator object. class( ode_container ), intent(inout) :: sys The ode_container object containing the ODE's to integrate. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: h The current step size. real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x The current value of the independent variable. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y The current value(s) of the dependent variable(s). real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(:) :: f An N-element array containing the values of the derivatives\nat x.  For a system carrying a mass matrix these are the\nvalues of rather than of . real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: yn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nsolution estimate at x + h. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(:) :: fn An N-element array where this routine will write the next\nderivative estimate at x + h. class(*), intent(inout), optional :: args An optional argument that can be used to pass information\nin and out of the differential equation subroutine. Derived Types type, public, abstract, extends( ode_integrator ) :: multistep_integrator Defines the structure of a multi-step integrator. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ode_event_solver ), public :: event_solver The ODE event solver.  Enable event detection by defining the\nevent_function in the ode_container object. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: append_to_buffer => oi_append_to_buffer Appends the supplied solution point to the internal solution \nbuffer. procedure, public :: clear_buffer => oi_clear_buffer Clears the contents of the buffer. procedure, public :: compute_dense_output => mi_dense_output procedure, public :: compute_error_norm => oi_estimate_error Computes the norm of the scaled error estimate. procedure( multistep_corrector ), public, deferred, pass :: correct Refines the prediction by applying the implicit formula. procedure, public :: estimate_inital_step_size => oi_initial_step Computes an estimate of an initial step size. procedure, public :: estimate_next_step_size => oi_next_step Estimates the next step size. procedure, public :: evaluate_dense => oi_evaluate_dense Evaluates the prepared step without advancing integration. procedure, public :: evaluate_derivative => mi_evaluate_derivative Evaluates the derivative stored in the solution history. procedure, public :: get_absolute_tolerance => oi_get_a